The temperature decision now comes from yoagent's accepts_sampling_params, read off the config each agent is built from. yoyo's own Claude version parse is gone. Committed as 213c26c6; build, all tests, clippy -D warnings and fmt pass.

The plan was wrong about the bug. OpenRouter users weren't having their temperature silently dropped. yoyo builds the openrouter config with ModelConfig::openai, which leaves the flag on and never uses yoagent's openrouter preset. So an anthropic/claude-opus-5.5 user who set --temperature had it sent, and every call failed with HTTP 400. The Bedrock arm builds with ModelConfig::custom, which also leaves the flag on, so if I'd only swapped the check, Bedrock would have broken too.

What changed:
• `temperature_support.rs`: the version parse, FIRST_REJECTING_VERSION and rejects_temperature are deleted. effective_temperature now takes the built config's flag and still prints the stderr note once per process.
• `agent_builder.rs`:
  • The openrouter and Bedrock arms copy the flag from yoagent's config for the Anthropic model behind the id.
  • Every builder (main, side, architect, editor) passes the flag from its own config.
  • configure_agent gained a parameter for it; three existing tests got true.
• `repl.rs`: the startup banner's "(not sent)" label reads the same flag.

Owner's limits:
• Gateways (`custom` / `ollama` / unknown OpenAI-compatible): yoagent infers nothing there, and its function that decides from an id (takes_sampling_params, model.rs:1098) is pub(crate), so yoyo can't call it. I didn't re-add a version parse, so a Claude 4.7+ id behind a gateway still gets the temperature. That case is pinned in the test as a known limit, and I asked upstream on #1122 for the function to be exported.
• `/model`: switching rebuilds the config through build_agent, so the flag is read fresh. There's a test for it.
• Persisted configs: my grep found no place where yoyo loads a saved ModelConfig, so the "saved before 0.27.3 loads with the flag on" limit doesn't apply.

Tests: the new table covers provider × id with or without a temperature, all built through the real create_model_config.
• The openrouter anthropic/claude-opus-5.5 row failed before the change.
• Removing the openrouter copy, or the Bedrock copy, makes the table fail on the matching row. I ran each removal, test and restore as one command, and the file matched its backup afterwards.

docs/src/configuration/skills.md now names OpenRouter and the gateway limit. The commit is titled "Part of #1122" because the upstream ask is still open.
